        "original_id": "a458f21e-3bf5-5b1d-8ca8-1c033f323468",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Shihad, Morningwood\n- People: Pedro Yanowitz, Hayley Westenra\n- Companies: Capitol Records\n- Products: The General Electric\n- Places: New Zealand\n\nFacts:\n- In October 1999, Shihad released The General Electric as their fourth album.\n- During their recording career, Shihad produced five number-one studio albums in New Zealand.\n- Shihad held the record for the most number-one records by any New Zealand artist alongside Hayley Westenra.\n- Shihad also had three top-ten singles in New Zealand.\n- Morningwood was signed to Capitol Records.\n- Morningwood released two albums.\n- Pedro Yanowitz was the bass player, songwriter, and producer for Morningwood.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
